From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ali Hijazi <ahijazi@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:21:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] [3.1.1] [M156] [DBSC] Make session deletion re-entrancy safe

Original change's description:
> [DBSC] Make session deletion re-entrancy safe
>
> Deleting a session unblocks its deferred requests synchronously. A
> restarted request can re-enter SessionServiceImpl and delete other
> sessions before control returns, which invalidates iterators and
> references the caller still holds into `unpartitioned_sessions_`.
>
> - DeleteSessionAndNotifyInternal() now takes ownership of a node that
>   was already extracted from `unpartitioned_sessions_`. No references
>   into the map are held while callbacks run, and re-entrant calls can't
>   see the session being deleted.
> - DeleteAllSessions() and GetSessionsForSite() extract the sessions to
>   delete first and delete them afterwards. GetSessionsForSite()
>   recomputes the returned range after deleting.
> - ShouldDefer() iterates over a copy of the session keys, because
>   starting a proactive refresh can complete and delete a session
>   synchronously.
> - Refresh and key-restore failures that delete the session now remove it
>   before unblocking its waiting requests, so that restarted requests
>   can't see it either.
> - RefreshSessionInternal() no longer unblocks the waiting requests a
>   second time after OnSessionKeyRestored() has done so. That could fail
>   a request deferred re-entrantly in between, and later trip
>   CHECK(deferred_reqs) when that request's own key restore completed.
>
> A re-entrant deletion of a session that is already being deleted is now
> a no-op.
>
> Fixed: 575007933
> Test: net_unittests --gtest_filter='SessionServiceImpl*' under ASan
> Change-Id: Ic25433658c040d3d640a528b129e6d4ad0f93bc7
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8624547
> Commit-Queue: Ali Hijazi <ahijazi@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Alex Ilin <alexilin@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1736464}

(cherry picked from commit bd814c1eefaaf858f478420b9cbcb2db3d572d49)

Conflicts resolved in session_service_impl.cc and
session_service_impl.h: the conflicting lines are comments that
crrev.com/c/8520158 changed on main, and that CL is not on this branch.
The resolved code matches main. The branch keeps its own comments for
RestoreSessionKey() and OnSessionKeyRestored(), because on this branch
OnSessionKeyRestored() does not run its callback if the session was
deleted during the key restore.

StartSessionRefresh(): this branch does not have the key restore
priority from crrev.com/c/8422787, so the RestoreSessionKey() call keeps
its current arguments.

session_service_impl_unittest.cc: adds CreateRequestWithContext() and
the LoadSessionWithUnrestoredKey() fixture helper, which are not on this
branch, and the RestoreSessionBindingKey() expectations take no
priority.

Bug: 582594431,575007933
Test: net_unittests --gtest_filter='SessionServiceImpl*' (Linux ASan)
